# Synthetic-fixture allowlist, read by scripts/ci/check_synthetic_fixtures.py.
#
# Real session audio, transcripts, excerpts and feedback may never be committed, not even
# as test fixtures (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md section 7, docs/POLICY.md DAT-1 and DAT-6). A
# file the check flags may be listed here only if it is synthetic: generated or
# hand-written test data with no real student or session content.
#
# Format: one exact repository path, its git blob sha, then a justification comment.
#   tests/fixtures/sine-440hz.wav 0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef01234567  # synthetic: generated tone
# Get the blob sha after staging the file: git ls-files -s -- <path> (the second column).
# Changing the file changes its sha, so the entry must be updated and reviewed again.
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored. Paths may not contain "#".
# A malformed entry, an unjustified entry, or an entry for an untracked path fails the check.
# gitleaks suppression files (.gitleaks.toml, .gitleaksignore) can never be listed here.
#
# CODEOWNERS requests the owner's review of every change to this file. GitHub enforces
# that review only once the rulesets turn on "Require review from Code Owners".
